14. Glassmorphism and surface treatments
The glassmorphism is not identical across every component.

The main hero card has a photographic background.

The weather card has a relatively dark green surface.

The irrigation card has a brighter emerald tint.

The soil card uses a dark glass surface.

The alerts card uses a darker, more muted appearance.

All of them share the same underlying visual language.
Reusable glass CSS
.glass-panel {
    position: relative;

    background: rgba(5, 40, 26, 0.72);

    backdrop-filter: blur(20px);
    -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(20px);

    border: 1px solid rgba(120, 204, 146, 0.26);

    border-radius: 20px;

    box-shadow:
        inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255,255,255,0.07),
        0 8px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.16);
}


Green illumination
Use soft radial gradients behind the main panels.
.green-glow {
    box-shadow:
        0 0 25px rgba(0, 192, 89, 0.08),
        inset 0 0 20px rgba(0, 160, 82, 0.05);
}


Important rendering rule
Avoid making all cards equally bright.

The interface relies on varying levels of darkness to establish visual hierarchy.

The crop photograph and green irrigation card are among the more prominent visual regions.

The alert and rotation cards are more subdued.

