18. Responsive behavior
The reference is a desktop dashboard, but the design should adapt to different viewports.
Desktop — 1440 px and above
- Hero card spans full width.
- Four hero regions remain horizontal.
- Weather and irrigation panels sit side by side.
- Bottom section uses three columns.
- All content is visible without horizontal scrolling.
Laptop — 1024–1439 px
- Hero sections remain horizontal if sufficient width exists.
- Weather and irrigation panels remain side by side where practical.
- Bottom cards can use a slightly adjusted three-column grid.
- Some supporting text may wrap.
Tablet — 768–1023 px
- Hero card can become two rows.
- Crop photograph and identity occupy the first row.
- Lifecycle and health information occupy the second.
- Weather and irrigation cards can stack.
- Bottom panels use two columns.
Mobile — below 768 px
- Breadcrumb becomes compact.
- Hero becomes a vertical card.
- Crop photograph appears at the top.
- Crop identity follows.
- Lifecycle data becomes a two-column metric grid.
- Health becomes a separate section.
- Weather occupies full width.
- Irrigation occupies full width.
- Soil information becomes vertical.
- Action plan occupies full width.
- Alerts and crop rotation stack vertically.
Do not force the original desktop dimensions onto mobile.

